{
  "reasoning": "REST API and GraphQL API differ in their approach to data retrieval and manipulation. A REST API uses a stateless, client-server architecture where the client sends HTTP requests to the server to retrieve or manipulate data, whereas a GraphQL API uses a query language to specify the data needed and the server responds with the requested data in a single response. This difference in architecture allows GraphQL APIs to provide more flexible and efficient data retrieval, as well as improved performance and scalability.",

